eserve my high cards (K, A, 2) for critical moments\n- With 11 cards, my teammate needs more opportunities to play out their hand\n- The landlord with only 7 cards is the immediate threat\n\nReason:\nI should **pass**. My teammate just played ♥Q, and by passing, I allow their card to win the trick, giving them control of the next lead. This is strategically sound because: (1) my teammate has the most cards (11) and needs opportunities to play them out, (2) I preserve my strong cards (K, A, 2) for blocking the landlord\'s plays later, (3) letting my teammate lead allows them to choose the combination type, which may help them reduce their hand more effectively.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
